1
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:51,000
My Little Pony: Equestria Girls - Spring Breakdown is a action,
adventure, comedy film directed by Ishi Rudell.

2
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
The Equestria Girls spend their spring break on a yacht.

3
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:21,000
It's Spring Break and the Mane 7 are about to board the most
glorious yacht ever for a relaxing cruise.

4
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
But Rainbow Dash is convinced that Equestrian Magic is on the
loose and won't let anyone rest until she finds it.

5
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Rainbow Dash / Applejack (voice), played by Ashleigh Ball.

6
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Pinkie Pie / Fluttershy (voice), played by Andrea Libman.

7
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Twilight Sparkle / Princess Twilight Sparkle (voice), played by Tara Strong.

8
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Sunset Shimmer / Twilight Sparkle (singing voice), played by Rebecca Shoichet.

9
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Rarity (voice), played by Tabitha St. Germain.

10
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Spike (voice), played by Cathy Weseluck.

11
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:21,000
My Little Pony: Equestria Girls – Spring Breakdown is a 2019 animated television special within Hasbro's My Little
Pony: Equestria Girls franchise, itself a spin-off of the 2010 relaunch of the My Little Pony toy line.

12
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
The special was directed by Ishi Rudell and Katrina Hadley, written and edited by Nick
Confalone, and produced by DHX Media Vancouver for Hasbro Studios in the United States.

13
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:51,000
Premiered on Discovery Family (a joint venture between Discovery, Inc.

14
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
and Hasbro) on March 30, 2019, it is the third one-hour Equestria Girls special, following Forgotten Friendship and Rollercoaster of Friendship
(both 2018), and preceding Sunset's Backstage Pass and Holidays Unwrapped (released later in July and November, respectively).

15
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
The tone is lighthearted.
